From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve exact traditional build-helper author and grant

Provenance: fixed official Module-Build 0.25 / Compat 0.03 and Class-Can 0.01.
Only add the original author/license declarations for the matched template;
no source code, default test or existing notice changes. Not RISC-V specific.
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (local packaging license preservation)

--- /dev/null
+++ b/BUILD-HELPER-LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Build-helper provenance and original licensing declarations
+
+Makefile.PL is traditional output of Module::Build::Compat 0.03, shipped in
+Module-Build 0.25. Exact official source:
+https://cpan.metacpan.org/authors/id/K/KW/KWILLIAMS/Module-Build-0.25.tar.gz
+SHA-256: cfda8575e400bf42fab7ad05eb7bffeeff1f51b161a18962c2adfd9a1395b6c8
+
+Original author declaration (lib/Module/Build/Compat.pm):
+Ken Williams, ken@mathforum.org
+
+Original license declaration (Build.PL):
+   license => 'perl',
+
+Original distribution metadata (META.yml):
+name: Module-Build
+version: 0.25
+author:
+  - Ken Williams, kwilliams@cpan.org
+license: perl
+
+Original meaning of that license option (lib/Module/Build.pm, item perl):
+The distribution may be copied and redistributed under the same terms
+as perl itself (this is by far the most common licensing option for
+modules on CPAN).  This is a dual license, in which the user may
+choose between either the GPL or the Artistic license.
+
+This packaging addition preserves the exact author/license declarations; it
+does not create a new grant, claim an independent upstream LICENSE file, or
+infer that generated or copied code is free of copyright. The original
+Class::Can source, code, default tests and existing notices are unchanged.
